Hand-port of upstream (github.com/jca02266/lha) security fixes to
lha-1.14i-ac20050924p1.  Upstream commits, adapted to p1's K&R layout:

  71ff940  huf.c read_c_len: bound zero-run expansion to NC (CVE-2006-4338)
  bf2471f  header.c level 0/1: reject too-small header size before fread
  2f6c23d  header.c: negative skip_bytes() length is an error
  cc2a649  header.c: negative get_bytes() length is an error
  bc618e1  header.c: get_byte() bounds-checked against the header buffer
  2602cd5  header.c level 2/3: validate header size and padding
  82efba6  header.c get_bytes(): never copy more than the destination size
  d00c5e9  lhext.c: refuse to extract through an existing symlink
           (+ util.c xsnprintf() returns the length written)
  b662b83  lhext.c: `lha p' must not create symlinks/directories
  43dede0  lharc.c include_path_p(): fix end-of-string test
  5fa932b  lhext.c: abort when seeking to the next header fails
  0f89645  bitio.c fillbuf(): abort on read error/EOF
  (is_symlink() guard for systems without S_IFLNK, from 86ef0f5)

